A||||4||John Jenkins||My '84 won't start - HELP!
Z||000000||John Jenkins||05-10-99||04:05 PM||||Hi!<br>I've recently purchased a 1984 Fiero SE.  For 3 1/2 days.  Today I began to drive home from school when after about 5 minutes my car shuttered back and forth a little and cut off.  I can't start the car.  The Interior lights still come on and the needles on the gauges move.  I can't open the trunk to look at the engine because the lock on the outside is broken and the inside button won't open.  Please, someone help me!  If there are any suggestions please e-mail me at JenksII@hotmail.com.  Thank you!
Z||000001||PaUL||05-10-99||04:21 PM||||You can use a flathead screwdriver to open the back. Stick in the hole where the key used to go, turn to open.
Z||000002||overlord||05-10-99||04:52 PM||||fuel pump??<br>ignition??<br>plugs?<p>hard to know if u cant look under the hood eh?
Z||000003||Patrick||05-10-99||05:22 PM||||<br>I think the squirrels may have died.  <IMG SRC="http://home.att.net/~albpm/smile2.gif"> <p>
Z||000004||theogre||05-10-99||10:05 PM||||assuming the solinoid in the trunk is connected, and good, there are 3 other things to check to get a power release to work. ((the solinoid gets unpluged by people who don't like the security problem the option causes.))<p>1. does the dome light come on? (the overhead light above the windscreen) if it does then the fuse is good. if not replace the fuse... it controlls part of the trunk latch as well.<p>2. the relay for this system is located under the dash directly below the trunk switch. It's a small square can. pull the horn relay from next to the blue box under the pasengers side of the dash and put it in to the trunk relay socket. if it works now the relay is bad. get another horn relay. the horn relay is heavier duty than the normal trunk one.<p>3. make sure the car is in park if it's an automatic. on my 87 the trunk will not open if it's not in park. push the shifter all the way up into park, and hit the button.
